==French==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/kɔ.pɛ̃/|lang=fr}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|fr}} {{m|fro|compaing}}, {{m|fro|compain}}, from {{etyl|LL.|fr}} {{m|la|compāniō}} (nominative form) (compare also Italian {{m|it|compagno}}), from {{prefix|com|pānis|lang=la|nocat=1}} (literally, [[with]] + [[bread]]), a word first attested in the {{etyl|frk|-}} ''Lex Salica'' as a translation of a Germanic word, probably {{etyl|frk|fr}} {{m|frk|*galaibo}}, {{m|frk|*gahlaibo||messmate|lit=with-bread}}, from {{m|frk|*hlaib||loaf, bread}}. See also {{m|fr|compagnon}}, from the accusative form of the same Late Latin term (''compāniōnem''), from whence also English {{m|en|companion}}. The boyfriend meaning is by ellipsis of {{m|fr|petit copain}}

===Noun===
{{fr-noun|m|f=copine}}

# (male) [[friend]], [[chum]], [[mate]] (''UK''), [[pal]], [[buddy]]
# {{lb|fr|informal}} [[boyfriend]] {{gloss|boy/man to which one has a romantic attachment}}

